        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="AbJ37FA1o0RB3voxti96-24" parent="x-8thJ_eOBKoUWWDrhoA-1" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" value="&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;Key Video Streaming Terminology&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Transcoding:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The process of converting a video file from one format, size, or bitrate to another (e.g., converting a massive &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.mov&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; camera file into a compressed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.mp4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; web video).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Bitrate:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The amount of data processed per second of video, usually measured in Megabits per second (Mbps). Higher bitrates yield better quality but result in larger file sizes and slower loading times.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;HLS (HTTP Live Streaming):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; An adaptive video streaming protocol developed by Apple. Instead of playing one giant file, it splits the video into tiny pieces and delivers them dynamically based on the viewer&#39;s internet speed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Segments (Chunks):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The tiny, individual video files (usually 2 to 10 seconds long, ending in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.ts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; or &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.m4s&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;) that make up an HLS stream.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Manifest File (&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; A text-based playlist file acting as an index or map. The video player reads this file to know exactly which video chunks to download and play next.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;Adaptive Bitrate Streaming (ABR):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; The technology that automatically switches video quality (e.g., dropping from 1080p to 480p) mid-stream if a user’s internet connection slows down, preventing the video from buffering.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;hr style=&quot;height: 1px; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-style: solid none none; border-color: rgb(220, 223, 229) currentcolor currentcolor; border-image: none;&quot;&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;What AWS Elemental MediaConvert Does: Step-by-Step&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400; overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;AWS Elemental MediaConvert&lt;/span&gt; is a serverless, file-based video processing engine. When you feed it a raw video file from Amazon S3, it automatically executes the following six steps:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;1. Ingestion &amp;amp; Analysis:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; MediaConvert securely connects to your S3 Input Bucket and fetches the source video. It scans the file to read its blueprint, identifying its original resolution, frame rate, audio tracks, and color settings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;2. Decoding &amp;amp; Cleaning:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; It unpacks the compressed video into raw, uncompressed frames. During this stage, it applies automatic filters to clean up the video if needed—such as fixing interlaced lines from older cameras or adjusting frame rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;3. Multi-Resolution Transcoding:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; MediaConvert duplicates the raw video frames and compresses them into multiple resolutions and bitrates simultaneously (e.g., 1080p, 720p, and 480p) based on your configurations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;💡 Smart Savings (QVBR):&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; MediaConvert uses built-in AI called Quality-Defined Variable Bitrate. If a scene is simple (like a person talking against a plain background), it automatically lowers the bitrate to save you storage and bandwidth costs. It only spikes the bitrate during fast-moving action scenes where detail is needed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;4. Chunk Segmentation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Once the multiple resolutions are created, MediaConvert slices them into exact, bite-sized 6-second segments. It precisely aligns the starting point of each chunk across all resolutions. This ensures that if a player switches a user from 720p to 1080p, the transition happens instantly without a visual stutter.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;5. Manifest Compilation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; As it creates the chunks, it automatically writes the text-based map files:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Variant Manifests:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; It creates a playlist for each resolution (e.g., &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;video_1080p.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;), listing all its specific 6-second chunks in chronological order.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Master Manifest:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; It creates one overarching file (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;master.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;) that links all the variant playlists together. This is the main link you give to your video player.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;6. Secure Delivery to S3:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Finally, MediaConvert saves the entire package—the master manifest, the individual resolution manifests, and the hundreds of tiny segment chunks—straight into your S3 Output Bucket. Once the last file is uploaded, it fires a success signal and shuts down, costing you nothing until your next video upload.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;hr style=&quot;height: 1px; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-style: solid none none; border-color: rgb(220, 223, 229) currentcolor currentcolor; border-image: none;&quot;&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;Important Architectural Points&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;1. S3 Multi-Bucket Architecture &amp;amp; OAC Security&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400; overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0;&quot;&gt;To maintain security while allowing client uploads, you must separate your infrastructure into two distinct S3 buckets using completely different access control models:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The S3 Input Bucket (Bypasses OAC):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Purpose:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; Holds raw, full-length uploaded videos temporarily.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Access Control:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; Stays 100% private to the public internet. It does not use Origin Access Control (OAC).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Client Upload Mechanism:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; The frontend client uploads video chunks directly here by using temporary, short-lived Presigned URLs generated on-demand by your Node.js backend.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The S3 Output Bucket (Enforces OAC):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Purpose:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; Stores the processed HLS streaming segments (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.ts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;) and manifest playlists (&lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;.m3u8&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;) indefinitely.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Access Control:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; Locked down strictly with Origin Access Control (OAC). Direct internet access to this bucket is completely blocked.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-weight: inherit;&quot;&gt;Client Access Mechanism:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; The client never downloads files directly from this bucket. Instead, they request the stream via the CloudFront CDN URL. CloudFront uses its secure OAC service principal permissions to fetch and cache the chunks out of S3 on the user&#39;s behalf.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;2. Presigned URLs for Multipart Chunk Uploads&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400; overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0;&quot;&gt;When handling large video files via chunks, a single standard presigned URL is structurally insufficient.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The Architecture Rule:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; One single presigned URL cannot be reused to upload multiple independent chunks of a single file under S3 Multipart Upload.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The Implementation Flow:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The client initiates an upload request to your Node.js backend.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Your backend requests an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;UploadId&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt; from AWS S3 via &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;CreateMultipartUpload&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Your backend calculates how many chunks the file requires, generates a unique presigned URL for every single individual part (bound explicitly to its &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;partNumber&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;), and passes an array of these URLs back to the frontend.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The client uploads each chunk to its corresponding unique URL sequence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;3. Grace-Period Cron Logic &amp;amp; The Heartbeat Pattern&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-weight: 400; overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 16px 0;&quot;&gt;Running a simple time-of-day cron job to clear &lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;PENDING&lt;/code&gt; database records will accidentally corrupt and kill active, ongoing user uploads. Your automation must account for elapsed time thresholds.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The Grace-Period Query Fix:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; Your cleanup worker (e.g., an AWS EventBridge daily Lambda trigger) must evaluate both the upload status and the creation timestamp. It should only mark uploads as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;FAILED&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; if they are stuck in a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;PENDING&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; state &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; are older than a specific grace period (e.g., 2 hours).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); padding: 16px; display: flex; gap: 16px; overflow-x: auto;&quot;&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin: 0; overflow: auto hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-sql&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(128, 134, 139); font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;/* Safe execution: Leaves active uploads untouched */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); padding: 16px; display: flex; gap: 16px; overflow-x: auto;&quot;&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin: 0; overflow: auto hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-sql&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(147, 52, 230);&quot;&gt;UPDATE&lt;/span&gt; videos &lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); padding: 16px; display: flex; gap: 16px; overflow-x: auto;&quot;&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin: 0; overflow: auto hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-sql&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(147, 52, 230);&quot;&gt;SET&lt;/span&gt; upload_status = &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(24, 128, 56);&quot;&gt;&#39;FAILED&#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); padding: 16px; display: flex; gap: 16px; overflow-x: auto;&quot;&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin: 0; overflow: auto hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-sql&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(147, 52, 230);&quot;&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; upload_status = &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(24, 128, 56);&quot;&gt;&#39;PENDING&#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); padding: 16px; display: flex; gap: 16px; overflow-x: auto;&quot;&gt;&lt;pre style=&quot;margin: 0; overflow: auto hidden&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-sql&quot;&gt;  &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(147, 52, 230);&quot;&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt; created_at &amp;lt; NOW() - &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(147, 52, 230);&quot;&gt;INTERVAL&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(24, 128, 56);&quot;&gt;&#39;2 HOURS&#39;&lt;/span&gt;;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0px 0px 0px 40px; border-width: medium; border-style: none; border-color: currentcolor; border-image: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;The Heartbeat Optimization:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; For users with slow network conditions uploading massive files over several hours, you can pivot the query to check an &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;updated_at&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; column instead. Every time the frontend successfully pushes a chunk, it hits a minor backend endpoint to refresh the video record&#39;s &lt;/span&gt;&lt;code dir=&quot;ltr&quot; style=&quot;color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal; background-color: rgb(244, 246, 247); border: 1px solid rgb(244, 246, 247); border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px;&quot;&gt;updated_at&lt;/code&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt; timestamp. The cron job then only cancels uploads if there has been absolute zero activity for a continuous 2-hour window.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); font-size: 12px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;Important Links&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-javascript/v3/developer-guide/emc-examples-jobs.html (link for mediaconvert processing&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mpuoverview.html (multipart upload)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12px; font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;hr style=&quot;height: 1px; border-width: 1px 0px 0px; border-style: solid none none; border-color: rgb(220, 223, 229) currentcolor currentcolor; border-image: none;&quot;&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot; role=&quot;heading&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;" vertex="1">
